WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:02.830
What happened in the Void Century?

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.540
What is the Will of D?

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.610
What actually is the One Piece?

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.230
Five years.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.450
One saga.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.500
It’s hard to believe that One Piece is coming
to a close soon.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.550
Allegedly at least.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:23.509
With 25 years of publication, it started to
seem like the story would go on forever, but

00:00:23.509 --> 00:00:28.810
all good things must come to an end, even
if Oda is being a little bit…optimistic

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.589
with his estimates.

00:00:30.589 --> 00:00:38.330
However, what’s even harder to believe is
how many questions we still have.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.830
How many mysteries still need solving.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:46.430
How many people, and places, and events we
still have to see in the story.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:55.440
In fact, today we have 146 things we need
to see before the end of One Piece.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.460
Let’s start with what many fans think will
be the setting of the next arc.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.120
We still need to see Elbaf, the Land of Giants.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.380
And concerning Elbaf, we still have a few
questions…like Who is Loki, the prince that

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.000
Big Mom mentioned on Whole Cake Island who
Lola was engaged to?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.710
Will we meet other Norse Mythology inspired
characters like Thor or Odin?

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.100
Well, actually I guess we already met Oden
on Wano.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.640
That might be too many Odens for one story.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.300
In Big Mom’s flashback, we also saw what
appeared to be a massive tree on the island.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.729
Is this the fabled Adam Tree?

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.810
We also know that while the giants have a
strong connection to Norse mythology, a certain

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:42.440
red-haired pirate who needs to reunite with
Luffy also has a Viking inspired ship, so

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.460
we have to ask: What is Shanks’ connection
to Elbaf?

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:51.760
And before we reach our final destination,
Laugh Tale, we’re still missing one road

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.000
poneglyph.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:03:07.650
Is it 
on Elbaf?

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:12.760
Speaking of Laugh Tale, though, we obviously
have a load of questions about this mysterious

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.769
island as well!

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:16.450
The first being…well…where is it?

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:21.760
And what was so outrageously funny that it
ended up with “laugh” in its name?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.269
Why exactly was Roger “too early” in arriving
there?

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:32.299
Elbaf and Laugh Tale are the two islands that
the Straw Hats absolutely, 100% need to visit

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:34.340
before the end of One Piece.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.819
However, there are still loads of other locations
that we’re wondering about.

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:45.739
One place we need to learn a lot about is
God Valley, but we’ll probably only learn

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:47.239
about it through flashbacks.

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:53.969
We probably won’t visit this location on
account that it completely disappeared, which

00:03:53.969 --> 00:04:00.849
raises the important questions “what happened
on God Valley?” and “why did it vanish?”

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:05.099
These three One Piece locations are far from
the only places we still have questions about:

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:09.230
Other places we’re still curious about,
but aren’t necessarily likely to get answers

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:14.939
before the end of the series include: Lodestar
Island and the mystery of its importance in

00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:20.669
teaching pirates about the poneglyphs; the
fabled Emerald City, a mythic place on par

00:04:20.669 --> 00:04:28.020
with Skypiea; and where and what was the thing
that we saw sucking Capone Bege and the Firetank

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.889
pirates into the sky?

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:35.030
Also - before we saw Buggy get imprisoned
in Impel Down he was searching for Captain

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.030
John’s treasure.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.560
Where and what is that treasure?

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.919
Does it have anything to do with his recent
promotion to Yonkou?

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:45.942
Oh also, quick shout out to Vin and Tuvillo,
the 2 subscirbers of the day, both of whom

00:04:45.942 --> 00:04:48.860
have helped to increase our bounty by 100
Berries each, once again taking a big step

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.560
towards 100M berries and overtaking Trebol.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.190
And it’s not just places we haven’t seen
that we have questions about…what about

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.510
questions we have about islands we have been
to!

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:58.510
Questions like:

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:00.830
Why is it always day on Enies Lobby?

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.479
How were the gates of justice constructed?

00:05:03.479 --> 00:05:07.850
(my vote goes to the unspeakable power of
awakened Blueno)

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:12.389
What were the giant silhouettes we saw in
the Florian Triangle?

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:15.770
Where are they building the bridge on Tequila
Wolf to?

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:18.900
How will Luffy destroy Fishman Island?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.689
What happened during the Reverie on Mariejois?

00:05:21.689 --> 00:05:23.800
How was the Red Line created?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:28.870
What was Zunisha’s punishment that lead
to Zou moving around for centuries?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.580
Why were Wano’s borders closed?

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:35.290
And let’s not forget the ever important
MOON.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:40.360
You know, sometimes I feel bad for anime only
watchers…because they don’t get to ask

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.569
questions like:

00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:43.320
Why are there seven moons?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.870
Are the sky islanders from the moon?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.810
What is Eneru doing up there with the space
pirates and army of automatons?

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:52.320
Okay, let me catch my breath.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.229
That’s 31 questions for those of you keeping
score and those are only questions about the

00:05:57.229 --> 00:05:59.509
geography of One Piece.

00:05:59.509 --> 00:06:05.730
But what about the over 1,000 characters of
One Piece - well, we have plenty of questions

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:06.750
about them, too!

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.750
Some important characters exist only in legend
- we haven’t even seen them and yet they

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:14.400
have an impressive presence in the series.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.410
The first that comes to mind is Rocks D. Xebec.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.490
Who is he?

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:19.520
What was his goal?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.689
How did he gather such a powerful crew?

00:06:22.689 --> 00:06:24.729
And what was his ultimate fate?

00:06:24.729 --> 00:06:29.879
And what about the greatest scientific mind
of the world government - the creator of the

00:06:29.879 --> 00:06:33.060
pacifistas and the artificial devil fruits.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.300
Who is Dr. Vegapunk?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:38.789
On the somewhat less important side, though,
we also have Scopper Gaban.

00:06:38.789 --> 00:06:42.100
Where is the Pirate King’s third in command?

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.479
Was he Crocus’s mysterious samurai friend?

00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:48.060
And finally…who is Charlotte Snack?

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:53.270
There is a whole Sweet Commander that we just
never got to see on Whole Cake Island!

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:57.660
And while we’re super curious about these
mysterious figures who’ve yet to be properly

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:03.009
introduced, we’re also missing some of our
old friends that we just know will play a

00:07:03.009 --> 00:07:05.159
role in the story to come.

00:07:05.159 --> 00:07:09.960
Some of these we’re bound to hear from very
soon and others we might be waiting a while,

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.070
but in the meantime we have to ask:

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.240
What happened to Sabo?

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.590
What happened to Vivi?

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:16.770
What happened to Moria?

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.539
What’s the status of the shichibukai who
were being hunted by the world government

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:23.650
- So where’s Mihawk?

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:25.840
Where’s Boa Hancock?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.409
What about Weevil?

00:07:27.409 --> 00:07:30.940
And is Edward Weevil actually Whitebeard’s
son?

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:36.159
You have to admit that the mustache resemblance
is uncanny…

00:07:36.159 --> 00:07:40.990
And what about the people he’s pursuing
- where are the remaining division commanders

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.139
of the Whitebeard pirates?

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:46.219
What is Crocodile up to in the New World?

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:51.189
And what is the big secret from his past that
Ivankov threatened him with?

00:07:51.189 --> 00:07:56.499
Where is Urouge - the member of the Worst
Generation we probably know the least about.

00:07:56.499 --> 00:08:04.090
With all of his peers being really fleshed
out, surely he has a role to play in the future

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.090
as well.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:09.460
There are also some loose ends to tie up from
really recent arcs - some other characters

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.150
we’d still like to check up on.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.790
How will Charlotte Katakuri factor into the
future of One Piece?

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:19.270
Will he ally with Luffy in the final war?

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:24.439
What happened to the Fishman pirates after
Whole Cake Island - did they survive Big Mom’s

00:08:24.439 --> 00:08:25.449
onslaught?

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:30.360
What happened to Big Mom’s children who
came to wano after they were knocked off of

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.360
the waterfall…twice?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:36.730
Oh and speaking of Big Mom…are Big Mom and
Kaidou dead?

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:41.070
In most series this wouldn’t be a question,
given their current status of being submerged

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:47.140
in magma, but this is One Piece we’re talking
about and they might just have the Will of

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.410
P on their side.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.070
What about the characters we haven’t seen
in a realllllly long time?

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:55.570
We already mentioned Eneru a little bit when
we talked about the moon, but I’m talking

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:59.640
about even farther back than that - all the
way to East Blue.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.920
Where did Axe-Hand Morgan escape to after
his cover story?

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.920
When will Gin finally reunite with the crew?

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:10.490
When will we see the most important character
in the series, Gaimon, again?

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:14.770
(Probably on Laugh Tale, since he is the One
Piece).

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:18.980
And finally, in the character category, we
have plenty of characters who we have seen

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:24.500
at least relatively recently and who are certain
to play important roles in the final saga,

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.320
but who still have tons of mystery surrounding
them:

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.630
Most recently, we have Buggy.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.960
How did he become a Yonkou?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.690
And in Wano, we still have a lot of questions
about Toki.

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:42.570
Primarily, why did she jump into the future
from the void century in the first place?

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:46.850
What about Bonney and Kuma, who we saw in
the Reverie.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.250
What is their connection?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:54.000
We know Kuma was a revolutionary, but why
was his epithet “the tyrant” and why did

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.790
he agree to Vegapunk’s experimentation?

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:01.540
Since Bonney can manipulate her age, how old
is she really?

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.030
Who is she, really?

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:07.510
Speaking of Kuma, what about the enigmatic
leader of the Revolutionaries and Luffy’s

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.100
absentee father, Dragon?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.080
Why did he abandon his son?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.550
What is his goal as leader of the Revolutionary
Army?

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.270
And…what’s his devil fruit power?

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:22.470
The prevailing theory is that he holds the
wind fruit, but this has yet to be confirmed.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:28.450
And if Kaidou turned out to be a fish, then
who knows what misdirection Oda may be employing

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:29.450
here.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:32.350
What about the enemies of the Revolutionary
Army - the World Government?

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:38.120
There’s still a ton of mystery surrounding
this organization, as well.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.870
So before the end of the series we still need
to know: What is the SSG?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.910
Who is the leader of Sword?

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:49.440
Is Tashigi actually connected to Kuina in
some way, or is their resemblance simply a

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.440
coincidence?

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:56.720
How about the Admirals - Where in the world
did they conscript Fujitora and Ryukugyu from?

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:01.950
They’re absolute powerhouses that the government
just plucked from nowhere.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:08.270
The prevailing theory was that Fujitora was
from Wano…but that doesn’t seem likely

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.270
anymore.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.520
Will we get the backstory of any admirals?

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.430
Did Aokiji actually leave the marines or is
he just spying on Blackbeard?

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.320
Who are the Gorosei?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:23.450
We know virtually nothing about these shadowy
figures at the helm of the world government.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.080
How old are they actually?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:29.830
Do they have powers or do they serve in a
purely non-combative role?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:37.040
And then who is Imu, the true ruler of the
World Government?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.510
How old are they?

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.800
What powers do they have?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.500
And since we recently learned about the Gorosei’s
special secret friend, Shanks, we need to

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:51.440
ask - Why is he able to just waltz into Mariejois
for a meeting with the Gorosei?

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:55.830
Did he know the importance of the Nika fruit
when he stole it from the World Government?

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:59.450
What are his true intentions or allegiances?

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:02.010
How powerful is Shanks, really?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:08.040
And, perhaps the most pressing question of
all…is Shanks the father of Makino’s baby?

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.620
How about the man who left Shanks with his
trademark scar?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.450
Luffy’s biggest rival for the Pirate King’s
crown: Blackbeard.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:20.230
Before the end of the series, we still need
to know Marshall D. Teach’s backstory.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:27.300
What is his connection to Rocks, given that
he named his ship the Saber of Xebec?

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:33.970
Why does he know so much about the world and
what is his goal?

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:39.570
And of course, the most mysterious of all,
why doesn’t he sleep and how can he have

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.000
two devil fruit powers?

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:45.530
For those of you keeping track at home that
brings us to 90 mysteries yet to be solved

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.120
in the series, but we’re far from done!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:53.990
All of these people and places still don’t
get to the core mysteries of One Piece - What

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.450
is the true history of this world?

00:12:57.450 --> 00:13:01.050
We still need to know what happened in the
void century.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.230
What is the true past of the World Government?

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:07.370
And what was the Ancient Kingdom that they
clashed with?

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:11.540
What was the great cleansing that led to the
presumed end of this kingdom?

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:17.220
In Wano, we learned a whole lot about Luffy’s
devil fruit, but for every answer we received,

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.730
we had more questions pop up in their place.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:27.120
Luffy is definitely the next Joyboy, but we
still have to wonder…Who was Joyboy?

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:32.200
And did the giant straw hat in Mariejois belong
to him originally?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.930
We know now that Luffy’s fruit wasn’t
actually the Gomu-Gomu no Mi.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:42.530
It turned out to secretly be the Hito Hito
no Mi: Model Nika all along - but who or what

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.780
is the Sun God Nika?

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:50.250
And speaking of his very special fruit, we
still need a certain Dr. Vegapunk to explain

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:55.710
to us what exactly devil fruits are in the
first place!

00:13:55.710 --> 00:14:01.070
What about Luffy’s other special powers
that go beyond his amazing feats of Haki or

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.660
Devil Fruit usage.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:08.750
What is the Will of D and the secret behind
his and so many other characters' mysterious

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:09.950
middle initial?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:14.440
What is the voice of all things and why can
Luffy hear it?

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:19.110
Thanks to Sukiyaki and Robin’s conversation
in the latest chapter, we also just learned

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:25.780
that the Ancient Weapon Pluton is located
in Wano, paying off a mystery that was introduced

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.730
all the way back in Alabasta!

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:34.390
We’ve learned quite a bit about Shirahoshi
AKA Poseidon, but what are the ancient weapons?

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.140
What was their purpose?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:40.630
We know that Pluton is a battleship of some
kind, but who created it?

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:46.000
And while we’re at it, who created the other
mysterious, massive boat, the Noah?

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:50.850
And for as much as we’ve heard about Pluton
and Poseidon, we’ve learned absolutely nothing

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.250
about Uranus.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:56.000
What and where is this final ancient weapon?

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:01.700
And, of course, we’re missing the ultimate
mystery - the treasure Luffy has been searching

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:05.480
for since Chapter 1.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.760
What is the One Piece?

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:13.510
Before our final category, there are some
other miscellaneous things that simply need

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.790
to happen before the end of the series.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:19.050
We need to know what the egg was on the Oro
Jackson!

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:24.500
We need to see the Ope-Ope no Mi’s immortality
surgery come into play.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.570
We need to see the Grand Fleet reappear in
the final war.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:33.260
And there are a few things that aren’t super
necessary, but we’d really, really, really

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:37.290
like to see them, so get your pen and paper
and start writing those letters to Oda!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:42.750
A lot of fans would love to see another Davy
Back Fight with higher stakes.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:47.360
We’d also like to see the Thousand Sunny’s
Klabautermann make an appearance.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:53.600
And while we are now in the era of God Usopp,
what I wouldn’t do to see Sogeking just

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:56.370
one last time before the end.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:16:00.630
People really want to see God Valley, but
I’m partial to Sniper Island.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:06.050
Hey, if they made it to Skypiea, surely the
Straw Hats can make it…into your heart.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:10.890
This brings us to a whopping 115 mysteries
we need solved and things we need to see in

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.360
the final saga of One Piece.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:19.050
But there’s one category to go: Things we
still need resolved with the Straw Hat crew

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.050
themselves.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:24.090
We’ve spent 25 years following the adventures
of Luffy and his crew.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:28.760
Each of the Straw Hats has a dream and we
just know we’ll see them achieve their goals

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.410
by the end of One Piece.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:35.420
For Roronoa Zoro, we still haven’t gotten
an explanation about his missing eye.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:40.990
We also got some massive hints, but no confirmation
that he has relatives in Wano.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:45.950
Oda went out of his way to deny that Zoro’s
father was Ushimaru, the Daimyo of Ringo…but

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.380
if not Ushimaru, then who?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:52.750
And now that he’s been wielding Oden’s
black blade, Enma, we’d love to see him

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:55.250
forge a black blade of his own.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:59.010
Oh, and what was with his standoff with the
Grim Reaper?

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:03.380
Of course, now that he’s presumably conquered
death, he still has an even more formidable

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.790
foe to defeat.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:10.530
Before the end, we need to see Zoro take on
Mihawk and become the greatest swordsman in

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:11.620
the world.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:14.470
Usopp also has plenty of goals to accomplish.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.550
He has plenty of lies that have yet to come
true.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:23.880
We’d love to see him leading a force of
8,000 men (preferably giants), become a true

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:27.600
warrior of the sea, and reunite with his father,
Yasopp.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.810
The chef of the crew, Sanji, still owes us
some answers as well.

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:36.100
His explanation is his burning passion and
many theorists think it has something to do

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:43.190
with Lunarian DNA, but we still need a straightforward
explanation of why Sanji can conjure fire.

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:49.910
And for someone so obsessed with romance,
will he ever find love and reunite with Viola

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.100
or Pudding?

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:55.650
But more important than his love for women
is his love for cooking, so we need to see

00:17:55.650 --> 00:18:00.120
him finally find the sea he’s always dreamed
of: the All Blue.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:05.470
We don’t have too many questions about Nami,
but given that she was adopted after being

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:10.800
found by Bellemere, we could still ask where
she’s originally from and who her parents

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:11.800
are.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.090
It doesn’t really matter, but given that
we’ve gotten a lot of extra backstory for

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:21.850
Sanji and Zoro and everybody on our crew seems
to secretly have special parents, it could

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:22.850
still happen.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:27.220
But what absolutely needs to happen is that
Nami needs to achieve her dream of completing

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.880
a map of the world!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:32.770
With Chopper, we have a few questions about
his zoan fruit.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:37.470
A lot of theorists speculate that his monster
point is a forced awakening, but we could

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.030
still use confirmation from Oda.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:44.430
Also, given that we’ve only ever really
seen him as a human/reindeer hybrid, we have

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.270
to ask: Can Chopper go full human?

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:53.870
I don’t want to see it because it would
be uncanny and terrifying, but I have to ask.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:58.380
By the end of the series, though, our favorite
doctor needs to cure the world’s diseases.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:03.750
Maybe he won’t get every single one, but
a great one for him to cure would be the laughing

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:09.220
side effects of the Smile fruits, allowing
him to further restore the Country of Wano.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:13.761
With Robin, most of her big mysteries were
already covered in the section about the True

00:19:13.761 --> 00:19:17.460
History, since her dream is to…uncover the
True History.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:21.820
However, there is a very pressing question…where
is her cowgirl hat?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:26.160
We can only pray that her signature hat makes
a return in the Final Saga.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:30.860
In order for us to uncover all that true history,
she also needs to find the remainder of the

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.550
poneglyphs and decipher them!

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:39.000
Given that we only just now found out what
the first poneglyph we saw in Alabasta said,

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:43.740
it would be really nice if Oda could give
us some translations of the other poneglyphs

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.740
as well.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:49.590
Franky isn’t too mysterious of a figure
- he kind of lets it all hang out.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:51.290
Sometimes a little too literally.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:56.510
But before the end of the series, we’re
sure to see him sail his dream ship, the Thousand

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.540
Sunny, around the globe.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:03.880
Brook, our favorite skeletal musician, obviously
has to reunite with Laboon, but we’d also

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:11.250
like to see how the #1 Bop, Bink’s Sake,
fits in with the One Piece, as has been highly

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.520
speculated.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:19.059
We don’t have too many questions about Jinbei,
but we do want to see him achieve his goal

00:20:19.059 --> 00:20:24.559
of brokering peace between Fishmen and humans,
as well as seeing fishmen return to the surface.

00:20:24.559 --> 00:20:28.440
We also don’t really have questions about
our new best friend Yamato…at least not

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.440
yet.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:34.410
But we do have some questions about our captain
- Monkey D. Luffy.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:38.280
Such as…who is his mom and is it Crocodile?

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:42.840
And while we’re at it, who’s his grandma,
because we don’t know who Dragon’s mom

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.930
/ Garp’s wife and/or partner was either.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:51.340
We also need to see him reunite with his mentor
Shanks, as well as return his signature Straw

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:57.150
Hat, in a moment that’s sure to leave fans
the world over in tears.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:02.910
We also need to find out what the mysterious
dream that he shares with Roger is.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:08.980
And, last, but certainly not least, we need
to see Luffy become the King of the Pirates.

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:13.580
Oh actually, for Luffy’s mom there is one
extrememly wild theory out there, that you

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.879
certainly shouldn’t miss!

